# AGENTS.md — {{ .DisplayName }}

This project was generated by **mcpgen v{{ .GeneratorVersion }}**. It is an MCP
server in Go built on `github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk` (MCP spec
2026-07-28). If you are an AI coding agent working in this repo, follow the
rules below.

## Layout and ownership

```
cmd/{{ .ServerName }}/main.go                 mcpgen-owned (entrypoint)
internal/mcpapp/mcpapp.go                     mcpgen-owned (server wiring)
internal/mcpapp/instructions.go               mcpgen-owned
internal/mcpapp/tools.go                      mcpgen-owned (registration + markers)
internal/mcpapp/prompts.go                    mcpgen-owned (registration + markers)
internal/mcpapp/resources.go                  mcpgen-owned (registration + markers)
internal/mcpapp/tools/handlers/<tool>.go     USER-owned (one file per tool)
internal/mcpapp/prompts/<prompt>.go           USER-owned
internal/mcpapp/resources/<resource>.go       USER-owned
mcpgen.json                                   mcpgen-owned (single source of truth)
.mcpgen/manifest.json                         mcpgen-owned (ownership + hashes)
Makefile, .github/workflows/ci.yml, server.json, AGENTS.md, README.md, Dockerfile, go.mod   mcpgen-owned
```

Rules:

1. **Never edit files marked `DO NOT EDIT region: mcpgen-owned`.** Regenerate or
   use `mcpgen add` instead.
2. **Never edit inside `// mcpgen:begin ...` / `// mcpgen:end ...` marker
   regions** in `internal/mcpapp/tools.go`, `prompts.go`, `resources.go`.
   `mcpgen add` inserts registrations there; if the markers are missing or
   hand-edited, `mcpgen add` exits 5 with a fix hint.
3. Handler/prompt/resource implementation files are **user-owned**: mcpgen
   never overwrites them after first generation (tracked via
   `.mcpgen/manifest.json` hashes).

## Adding a capability

Prefer the tool over hand-editing registration files:

```sh
mcpgen add tool tools/my_tool.json --dir . --json     # spec: {"id": "my_tool", "inputSchema": {...}}
mcpgen add prompt prompts/my_prompt.json --dir . --json
mcpgen add resource resources/my_resource.json --dir . --json
```

Then implement the stub in the new user-owned file.

## Verify until green

```sh
mcpgen check . --json
```

Exit 0 means green. Stages: `config → tidy → fmt → vet → build → test →
conformance` (conformance runs when node/npx are available and transport is
http; otherwise the stage is reported `skipped`). On failure the JSON envelope
contains `error.stage`, `error.code`, and `error.fix` with the file:line of the
first failure, plus `next_actions`. Loop: fix → `mcpgen check . --json` → repeat
until exit 0.

## Exit codes

| Code | Meaning |
|---|---|
| 0 | success |
| 1 | general failure (build/test/conformance) |
| 2 | usage error (bad flags/args) |
| 3 | dir exists without --force / not an mcpgen project |
| 4 | permission denied |
| 5 | conflict (duplicate id, markers missing) |
| 6 | prerequisite missing (go, node/npx) |

## House rules

- Keep generated servers on the pinned SDK version in `go.mod`; bump via mcpgen
  releases, not by hand.
- `make check` runs tidy → fmt → vet → build → test locally.
- `make conformance` runs the official MCP conformance suite against a local
  HTTP instance.
